  "enisaUuid": "91049f6a-7fd0-306f-a02b-742055132f8f",
  "description": "The fix for CVE-2026-55877 (GHSA-6v8j-33hc-mv84) sanitizes the SVG of icons before they are rendered inline. It removes scripts and event handlers everywhere, except inside <style> elements.\n\nUnlike in HTML, the content of an SVG <style> element is parsed as markup. An icon can therefore still run JavaScript in the page with, for example:\n\n<style><script>alert(1)</script></style>\n<style><img src=\"invalid:\" onerror=\"alert(1)\"/></style>\n\nApplications are exposed when an attacker can influence the SVG of the icons they render. The sources are the same as for CVE-2026-55877, like local icon files and the responses of the Iconify API.\n\n<style> elements are now sanitized like any other element, so their descendants lose scripts and event handlers. A <style> element that tries to close itself early is still removed. Otherwise, its CSS is kept.",
